WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.098 --> 00:00:06.308
It was March,

00:00:07.911 --> 00:00:09.121
the start of the pandemic.

00:00:10.706 --> 00:00:11.707
We didn't know anything.

00:00:13.398 --> 00:00:14.399
It was jam packed,

00:00:15.929 --> 00:00:16.930
business as usual. 

00:00:18.233 --> 00:00:19.234
People coughing,

00:00:20.395 --> 00:00:21.063
sweating,

00:00:22.077 --> 00:00:24.496
Some people even vomiting that their workstations,

00:00:25.042 --> 00:00:26.043
but we just kept working. 

00:00:27.503 --> 00:00:29.046
Because that's what we were told to do. 

00:00:30.677 --> 00:00:31.678
My name is Chris Smalls

00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:33.729
former Amazon employee 

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:36.727
fired on March 30th for holding a protest. 

00:00:41.226 --> 00:00:43.353
It all started when one of my colleagues got sick. 

00:00:44.628 --> 00:00:46.880
She was sneezing and had rosy cheeks. 

00:00:48.692 --> 00:00:49.693
As a fellow supervisor,

00:00:50.589 --> 00:00:51.590
I told her to go home.

00:00:52.284 --> 00:00:52.701
She did.

00:00:54.666 --> 00:00:57.169
Two hours later we had our daily sync meeting. 

00:00:57.836 --> 00:01:04.718
In this meeting I was told not to tell my employees 
that somebody tested positive for COVID-19, two weeks prior.

00:01:05.744 --> 00:01:08.455
After hearing that, that's when I took my stance.

00:01:09.223 --> 00:01:12.142
I went to tell my employees, what was really going on. 

00:01:13.273 --> 00:01:14.274
I also took action.

00:01:15.013 --> 00:01:19.977
On my own freewill I returned back to the building,
sat in the cafeteria for 10 hours a day,

00:01:20.636 --> 00:01:22.137
telling all day employees, the truth.

00:01:23.188 --> 00:01:23.941
[Smalls] Giselle, we six feet away?

00:01:23.941 --> 00:01:26.002
here, put your foot out.

00:01:26.009 --> 00:01:28.595
(scoffing) We're two feet away.

00:01:28.619 --> 00:01:30.829
[Smalls] Social distancing at it's best.

00:01:32.195 --> 00:01:36.491
From there, we marched into the general manager's office every morning 

00:01:37.578 --> 00:01:40.080
voicing our concerns to have our demands met.

00:01:40.309 --> 00:01:43.437
We wanted the building to be closed down, and sanitized.

00:02:32.532 --> 00:02:34.409
Just days after organizing,

00:02:35.243 --> 00:02:36.787
I was placed on a quarantine. 

00:02:38.025 --> 00:02:39.026
Not my friends,

00:02:39.379 --> 00:02:40.631
not my colleagues,

00:02:41.258 --> 00:02:42.843
not the person I ride to work with...

00:02:43.375 --> 00:02:44.293
just me.

00:02:46.393 --> 00:02:48.770
It was time to organize a real walkout. 

00:02:49.568 --> 00:02:53.780
[CNBC Anchor] At amazon.com's Staten Island fulfillment center in New York City,

00:02:53.874 --> 00:02:57.210
known as JFK8, plan to walk off-

00:02:57.294 --> 00:02:57.878
walk out

00:02:58.155 --> 00:02:58.614
walk out

00:02:58.871 --> 00:03:03.000
Amazon workers walked out of the fulfillment 
center warehouse on Gulf Avenue

00:03:03.018 --> 00:03:04.561
workers claim that the company-

00:03:04.561 --> 00:03:08.116
is mishandling its response to the covid 19 outbreak.

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:09.718
We just want the building to be sanitized. 

00:03:10.122 --> 00:03:13.030
Honestly it's not safe. It's nowhere near safe.

00:03:13.030 --> 00:03:14.448
This building needs to shut down.

00:03:14.595 --> 00:03:16.306
I saw people getting sick every single day. 

00:03:16.306 --> 00:03:19.365
I've been sending people home for differnet symptoms. 

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:22.442
We are the heart and soul of this building. 

00:03:22.479 --> 00:03:23.814
And they're going to treat us with respect.

00:03:24.878 --> 00:03:27.506
Two hours after the protest, I was terminated,

00:03:27.579 --> 00:03:32.709
over the phone, for violating the quarantine policy

00:03:32.709 --> 00:03:35.013
[PIX Anchor] 8:14 and this story getting a whole lot of attention.

00:03:35.013 --> 00:03:36.812
Amazon under fire this morning.

00:03:36.812 --> 00:03:39.940
[Inside Edition Anchor] This assistant manager who organized a mass walkout 

00:03:40.087 --> 00:03:44.132
at a distribution center on Staten Island, New York was fired today.

00:03:44.389 --> 00:03:47.851
Amazon said it was for allegedly breaking quarantine,

00:03:48.210 --> 00:03:50.045
not to get rid of a whistleblower.

00:03:50.065 --> 00:03:53.402
[John Oliver] But leaked notes from an internal meeting days later,

00:03:53.402 --> 00:03:55.163
which Bezos himself was present,

00:03:55.384 --> 00:04:01.348
show the company's leadership discussing plans to make Smalls, 
the face of the entire union organizing movement,

00:04:01.348 --> 00:04:04.282
since he is not smart or articulate.

00:04:07.705 --> 00:04:09.540
rven within the company.

00:04:08.912 --> 00:04:10.956
That memo pissed a lot of people off...

00:04:13.248 --> 00:04:19.051
Well my name is Tim gray and my title is unemployed bum, 
because I quit my job last May 1st.

00:04:19.381 --> 00:04:27.097
I used to be over at Amazon Web Services, 
my title there was vice president and distinguished engineer

00:04:27.097 --> 00:04:31.106
[News Anchor] Big business headline at home this morning
a Canadian vice president of Amazon 

00:04:31.106 --> 00:04:35.829
has resigned in protest over the company firing whistleblowers

00:04:35.829 --> 00:04:39.004
[Reporter] saying the company culture is just too toxic,

00:04:39.004 --> 00:04:41.516
When it came to firing whistleblowers,

00:04:41.516 --> 00:04:44.654
you know, the COVID came along,

00:04:44.654 --> 00:04:48.543
Amazon was spending huge amounts of 
money and effort trying to make warehouses safer,

00:04:48.543 --> 00:04:51.655
the workers were still scared about dying as a result of their work

00:04:51.655 --> 00:04:53.578
I had no trouble believing, two things at once

00:04:53.945 --> 00:04:56.281
that Amazon was working on it but it's still a big problem.

00:04:56.782 --> 00:05:00.994
And then they fired the activists who are trying to do something about it.

00:05:01.031 --> 00:05:03.325
You can't argue about firing activists

00:05:03.435 --> 00:05:05.062
it's just malevolent and unethical.

00:05:05.172 --> 00:05:08.258
And it's not a thing that I think, one should be asked to live with.

00:05:08.258 --> 00:05:10.062
And, you know, I had a VP rank

00:05:10.062 --> 00:05:12.704
and as a VP rank you sort of stand for the company 

00:05:12.924 --> 00:05:14.384
and I just couldn't be in tune with that.

00:05:14.751 --> 00:05:16.586
[Reporter] He said he's quiting in dismay

00:05:16.586 --> 00:05:19.521
He said that Amazon fired whistleblowers.

00:05:19.521 --> 00:05:20.672
And he's paying the price for it too. 

00:05:20.672 --> 00:05:24.718
He says he's gonna lose a million dollars 
in salary and stock options by making this move.

00:05:24.755 --> 00:05:27.591
And he says that if he didn't do anything, he would be complicit.

00:05:27.591 --> 00:05:30.617
At the moment we're doing the arithmetic of costs and benefits.

00:05:30.826 --> 00:05:36.790
The costs borne by the workers in the 
warehouses are just I don't think, adequately costed in.

00:05:36.973 --> 00:05:40.477
And the reason for that is simple is 
because they are relatively powerless.

00:05:40.749 --> 00:05:42.508
They are fungible, they can be replaced.

00:05:42.508 --> 00:05:49.682
you know, if one of them leaves, somebody else can be hired,
usually in pretty short order to replace them and get back on the air.

00:05:49.938 --> 00:05:54.562
So the real problem here is not a numbers problem,

00:05:54.562 --> 00:05:55.517
it's a power problem.

00:05:55.664 --> 00:05:59.918
It's the disparity in power between the very large, highly concentrated firms

00:06:00.212 --> 00:06:02.756
who dominate the heights of the big tech economy,

00:06:03.266 --> 00:06:05.894
and the people who do the entry level jobs.

00:06:06.336 --> 00:06:10.298
And I firmly believe that if you dislike the behavior of these companies,

00:06:10.747 --> 00:06:13.917
the only real solution for that is old fashioned politics to you know,

00:06:13.917 --> 00:06:15.183
find politicians and elect them,

00:06:15.799 --> 00:06:18.635
who will improve the regulatory and legislative framework,  

00:06:19.172 --> 00:06:23.051
so that the behaviors that irritate us, they're just no longer acceptable.

00:06:23.964 --> 00:06:27.551
So here is Jeff Bezos, his company, Amazon,

00:06:28.888 --> 00:06:31.516
and they received a tax rebate,

00:06:31.590 --> 00:06:35.594
they paid nothing in 2018 in federal taxes, 

00:06:35.887 --> 00:06:39.357
That's a corrupt tax system to begin with.

00:06:39.982 --> 00:06:45.931
But then on top of that, they received $129 million as a tax rebate.

00:06:46.401 --> 00:06:47.402
So Amazon isn't the problem

00:06:47.549 --> 00:06:49.468
the problem isn't that Amazon is evil.

00:06:49.468 --> 00:06:56.244
The problem is that we have accepted
a structure of legislation and regulation 

00:06:56.244 --> 00:06:58.520
that allows companies like Amazon, 

00:06:58.607 --> 00:07:01.484
to play entirely by the rules, break no laws,

00:07:02.035 --> 00:07:08.547
and still do things that when you're looking at them, seem like opression.

00:07:10.096 --> 00:07:11.620
[Smalls] They thought firing would put an end to me, 

00:07:12.758 --> 00:07:13.683
they were wrong. 

00:07:14.796 --> 00:07:15.505
[Smalls on megahpone] For those who don't know me,

00:07:15.634 --> 00:07:18.011
my name is Chris Smalls, former Amazon employee

00:07:18.029 --> 00:07:21.950
that was fired from Amazon back in March, March 30th,

00:07:21.950 --> 00:07:23.740
for raising health and safety concerns.

00:07:23.979 --> 00:07:28.900
And now we're here today, becuase
we're gonna march on this motherf***ing Jeff Bezos house today

00:07:28.937 --> 00:07:32.566
(crowd cheers)

00:07:32.632 --> 00:07:33.925
And this is what we're about,

00:07:34.329 --> 00:07:37.249
we are about giving the power back to the workers,

00:07:37.369 --> 00:07:39.037
putting the power into workers hands,

00:07:39.092 --> 00:07:42.012
and letting the workers decide their own destiny.

00:07:42.048 --> 00:07:43.341
(chanting) IF WE DON'T GET IT?

00:07:43.341 --> 00:07:44.181
SHUT IT DOWN!

00:07:44.181 --> 00:07:45.358
IF WE DON'T GET IT?

00:07:45.358 --> 00:07:46.499
SHUT IT DOWN!

00:07:46.499 --> 00:07:51.284
Me being a supervisor, pre COVID, building the foundation,

00:07:51.394 --> 00:07:55.148
the relationship with my employees, something family oriented,

00:07:56.024 --> 00:07:58.568
I carried that over into this organizing position.

00:07:59.808 --> 00:08:02.894
It was easy for me to transition into this position because

00:08:03.421 --> 00:08:09.177
Amazon ironically, pretty much prepped me 
for this for the last five years when I was employed.

00:08:09.206 --> 00:08:12.584
I've been a leader there, and when they terminated me,

00:08:12.767 --> 00:08:14.561
they got rid of one of their best leaders. 

00:08:14.814 --> 00:08:19.486
And they didn't know that. But I think they may know now.

00:08:19.486 --> 00:08:21.159
(chanting) IF WE DON'T GET IT?

00:08:21.159 --> 00:08:21.952
SHUT IT DOWN!

00:08:22.098 --> 00:08:24.893
IF WE DON'T GET IT?

00:08:24.893 --> 00:08:26.441
SHUT IT DOWN!

00:08:26.551 --> 00:08:28.637
I never planned on being the organizer.

00:08:29.856 --> 00:08:33.235
I was just a concerned supervisor looking out for people.

00:08:33.558 --> 00:08:35.185
And I'm going to continue to do that.

00:08:36.219 --> 00:08:38.430
since then, I've organized around the country.

00:08:39.883 --> 00:08:41.593
I founded my own organization

00:08:42.090 --> 00:08:43.842
The Congress of Essential Workers,

00:08:43.915 --> 00:08:44.838
T.C.O.E.W.,

00:08:45.519 --> 00:08:49.190
to continue to uplift the voices of all essential workers.

00:08:50.320 --> 00:08:51.905
[Michael Brooks] Welcome Chris Smalls. 

00:08:51.997 --> 00:08:54.958
He is organizing Amazon workers.

00:08:55.075 --> 00:08:56.701
[Amazon Worker] When it comes to profit over safety,

00:08:56.885 --> 00:08:57.886
they will always choose profit.

00:08:58.945 --> 00:09:00.614
[Celeste Huete] Pay your employess a living wage

00:09:00.632 --> 00:09:02.592
so they won't have to be on government subsidies.

00:09:02.857 --> 00:09:06.611
[Amazon Worker] If you go on the website, 
all the essential items are sold out.

00:09:07.127 --> 00:09:08.128
Until you restock, 

00:09:08.311 --> 00:09:09.604
shut it down! 

00:09:09.641 --> 00:09:11.434
{Former Amazon Worker] But you have a man that's a billionaire

00:09:11.618 --> 00:09:12.577
and then not being taxed

00:09:13.435 --> 00:09:15.145
What part of the game is that?

00:09:15.724 --> 00:09:17.559
Tell me, where the right and wrong is in that?

00:09:18.571 --> 00:09:21.199
[Smalls] I always say it's not gonna be Amazon versus Chris smalls...

00:09:22.736 --> 00:09:25.322
It's going to be Amazon versus the people.

